================================================================================
Third-party software
================================================================================

DigiPet is MIT. It also ships with, or may load, separate works. Those works
keep their own licenses. When more than one extra helper is loaded, every
listed license applies at the same time. DigiPet does not replace them.

Always present at runtime (bundled):

  Three.js
    License: MIT
    https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js

  Electron
    License: MIT
    https://github.com/electron/electron

Build-time tools (not required to run a packaged app):

  Vite
    License: MIT
    https://github.com/vitejs/vite

  TypeScript
    License: Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript

  electron-builder
    License: MIT
    https://github.com/electron-userland/electron-builder

Optional local chat sidecar (only if `digipet-engine` is built with cargo):

  Hugging Face Candle
    License: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
    https://github.com/huggingface/candle

  SmolLM2-135M-Instruct (GGUF)
    License: Apache-2.0
    https://huggingface.co/HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-135M-Instruct

OS helpers (loaded only when the user ticks them in setup or the tray):

  Weather helper (DigiPet)
    License: MIT
    Forecast data: Open-Meteo, CC BY 4.0
    https://open-meteo.com

  Mail helper (DigiPet)
    License: MIT
    Calls Apple Mail, Outlook, or xdg-email. Those apps keep their own terms.

  Calendar helper (DigiPet)
    License: MIT
    Calls Apple Calendar, Outlook, or khal. Those apps keep their own terms.

  Apps helper (DigiPet)
    License: MIT
    Opens or quits OS applications. Those apps keep their own terms.

  Messages helper (DigiPet)
    License: MIT
    Calls Apple Messages where available. That app keeps its own terms.

Open-Meteo data is CC BY 4.0 (attribution). It is forecast data over HTTPS,
not a library vendored in this tree. Apple Mail, Outlook, Calendar, Messages,
and similar OS apps are not part of DigiPet.

Direct runtime and sidecar dependencies are MIT or Apache-2.0 (Candle is dual
Apache-2.0 / MIT). No GPL libraries are included.
